# .env keys that are RETIRED: nothing reads them any more, so the stack is
# correct with or without the line, but the line does nothing.
#
# ONE source of truth, read by both:
#   - scripts/lib-addons.sh  warn_retired_env_keys  (the launcher's WARN)
#   - noo onboard --only env  (offers to remove them; noo-cli embeds this file)
#
# Format: KEY|what replaced it (one line; shown after "which is RETIRED and ignored —")
# Keys the launcher REFUSES on (NOO_*_ENABLED add-on flags) are not listed
# here: lib-addons.sh addons_guard_retired_flags owns those.
TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_USERS|it admits nobody. Who may talk to the bot is noo_user_channel_links: noo security user link <username> telegram <id>
NOO_VLLM_TLS|every backend door is mTLS unconditionally, and a false value makes the node agent refuse to start
NOO_LLAMACPP_TLS|every backend door is mTLS unconditionally, and a false value makes the node agent refuse to start
NOO_OLLAMA_TLS|every backend door is mTLS unconditionally, and a false value makes the node agent refuse to start
NOO_TEI_TLS|every backend door is mTLS unconditionally, and a false value makes the node agent refuse to start
NOO_RERANKER_TLS|every backend door is mTLS unconditionally, and a false value makes the node agent refuse to start
NOO_INTEL_IMAGE|a licensed add-on runs only the image its own signed lock pins (addons.lock, written by noo addons upgrade); there is no override
NOO_EVOLVE_IMAGE|a licensed add-on runs only the image its own signed lock pins (addons.lock, written by noo addons upgrade); there is no override
NOO_INTEL_IMAGE_PREFIX|the add-on registry comes from the entitlement's add-on trust block, and its images are pinned by digest (noo addons upgrade)
NOO_EVOLVE_IMAGE_PREFIX|the add-on registry comes from the entitlement's add-on trust block, and its images are pinned by digest (noo addons upgrade)
PAGEINDEX_LLM_URL|the worker's LLM calls go through the gateway as a purpose (knowledge, graph), mesh-routed with failover (i145)
PAGEINDEX_LLM_MODEL|which model serves trellion is a preference in the DB: noo cluster class set <class> <node>/<backend> --alias knowledge (undeclared = any live chat node) (i145)
NOO_TRELLION_LLM_URL|trellion's LLM calls go to the gateway address (NOO_TRELLION_GATEWAY_URL), as the knowledge purpose (i145)
NOO_SELF_CALL_SHARED_SECRET|the self-call bridge is deleted: a shared secret never buys inference (the gateway refuses it on /v1/* and /api/external/*), and every caller presents its own key: noo security service-key issue <consumer>
NOO_CLUSTER_TOKEN_V1|the v1 cluster-token gate is deleted: a v1 token (the old replayable form) is always refused, and nodes sign v2 only. Nothing reads the line; the stored posture row is deleted at the next gateway start
NOO_CONTROLLER_SSH_PUBKEY|the controller serves no SSH key: enrollment pins none, and the noo-gate lane it was for is retired (nodes collect CA-signed bundles over the pull rail)
